The Rust assertions, actual factory instrumentation, resource-free affine probe,
explicit typed cache interfaces, dense matrix oracles and historical Rust stream
capture are independent adaptations. The retained incremental-stream hashes
come from Rust commit fbe56895852a92afb547e15e6ef3a016c4b67917, not the upstream
Python MT19937 stream. Fixed-template and cold-prefix affine bases have distinct
seeded conventions. The source fixture records both.

Native private parent counts, Python graph identity and numeric exception ABI
are not copied as Rust guarantees. Prepared scalar geometry, resource ownership,
actual factory events, typed admission, caller-owned random words and actual
callbacks are checked explicitly. Retained classical-label distributions in the
shared query fixture are checked cell by cell using explicit scalar event rows.
